@copilot Update this PR directly to integrate the context regression coverage into existing tests instead of adding the 213-line JettyHttpClient9ContextTest class. Keep the TracingHttpClient production fix unchanged.

Prefer extending contentResponseBodyIsDelivered() in instrumentation/jetty-httpclient/jetty-httpclient-9.2/library/src/test/java/io/opentelemetry/instrumentation/jetty/httpclient/v9_2/JettyHttpClient9HttpCallTest.java, reusing its server, instrumented client, and cleanup. Capture Context.current() during synchronous destination preparation using the existing non-matching HttpProxy.matches hook, verify that it contains the actual outgoing CLIENT span, and verify that send() restores the caller context. Retain the existing response-body assertions. The inherited AbstractHttpClientTest callback tests already exercise callbacks with and without a parent, so avoid duplicating that coverage. Preserve distinct synchronous-exception context-restoration coverage as a compact method in an existing test class, and preserve no-started-span behavior coverage without duplicating server/client lifecycle setup. Remove JettyHttpClient9ContextTest.java rather than moving its entire contents wholesale into another class.

Keep the changes focused and materially smaller, with no new standalone context test class or unnecessary helpers. Run the narrowest relevant formatting and tests, and demonstrate that the delegated-send regression assertion fails without the production context scope and passes with it.

